\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Takeaway: repairing a matching metric destroys it while deepening a verification signal strengthens it, but the strengthened signal only converges toward the free bit from below.} Left: up-weighting late reference tokens decays \textsc  {TFA}'s twelve-model ranking signal past $\gamma {=}1$, through the answer-only-reference null and beyond it to $-0.37$ at last-four tokens (the decay is a trend, not strictly monotone: $\gamma {=}1$ ticks up to $+0.15$ and last-16 sits above $\gamma {=}8$); the registered call was a null, so the sign flip is a recorded miss. Right: the completion-curve signal rises with truncation depth in Pearson, from a pure difficulty probe at $k{=}0$ to $+0.78$ against human soundness at $k{=}0.75$; the dashed line marks the free bit ($+0.92$), which the curve never reaches, and the Spearman profile is non-monotone.}}{11}{figure.caption.25}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sweeps}{{3}{11}{\textbf {Takeaway: repairing a matching metric destroys it while deepening a verification signal strengthens it, but the strengthened signal only converges toward the free bit from below.} Left: up-weighting late reference tokens decays \tfa 's twelve-model ranking signal past $\gamma {=}1$, through the answer-only-reference null and beyond it to $-0.37$ at last-four tokens (the decay is a trend, not strictly monotone: $\gamma {=}1$ ticks up to $+0.15$ and last-16 sits above $\gamma {=}8$); the registered call was a null, so the sign flip is a recorded miss. Right: the completion-curve signal rises with truncation depth in Pearson, from a pure difficulty probe at $k{=}0$ to $+0.78$ against human soundness at $k{=}0.75$; the dashed line marks the free bit ($+0.92$), which the curve never reaches, and the Spearman profile is non-monotone}{figure.caption.25}{}}
